---
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";

const frontmatter = {
  title: "EuroStream — Build a GDPR-Compliant Real-Time Analytics Platform in Pure Python",
  description:
    "The engineering cookbook behind EuroStream — streaming fraud detection, a medallion warehouse, PII governance and a working GDPR Article 17 erasure cascade. Recipes, architecture decisions, production playbook and interview prep.",
  template: "splash" as const,
  hero: {
    title: "Build a GDPR-compliant real-time analytics platform",
    tagline:
      "The complete engineering cookbook behind EuroStream — event streaming, medallion warehouse, PII governance, and a right-to-erasure cascade that actually works. Every recipe explains the problem, the decision, the code, and the trade-offs.",
    actions: [
      { text: "Read the Cookbook", link: "/cookbook/", variant: "primary" },
      {
        text: "Why this architecture wins",
        link: "/deep-dives/why-this-architecture",
        variant: "minimal",
      },
    ],
  },
};
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <div class="sl-container landing">
    <section class="landing-intro">
      <p>
        Most demo pipelines stop at <em>Kafka → warehouse</em>. In the EU that
        is not enough: <strong>GDPR Article 17</strong> doesn't care how fast
        your pipeline is if you can't prove you deleted someone's data when
        they asked. EuroStream is the missing half — the governed data platform
        — built end-to-end in pure Python.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section">
      <h2>What you get from this cookbook</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>A working platform you can run on a laptop.</strong> Zero
          Docker for local dev, zero JVM, zero cloud spend.
          <code>uv run eurostream demo</code> executes the full loop: ingest →
          fraud scoring → medallion transform → erasure → verified audit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Eight recipes that each solve one hard problem properly</strong>
          — durable event logs without Kafka, windowed fraud rules without
          Spark, erasure cascades with tamper-evident audits, schema contracts
          enforced in CI.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Decision records, not just code.</strong> Every chapter
          answers <em>why this way</em>, <em>what was rejected</em>, and{" "}
          <em>what changes at scale</em>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Interview-grade understanding.</strong> A dedicated prep
          section with an elevator pitch, likely questions with strong answers,
          and honest trade-off sheets.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section">
      <h2>The platform in one diagram</h2>
      <pre><code>{` Source systems (simulated, pure Python)
      |  orders · clicks · payments
      v
 Event bus (durable append-only log; Kafka adapter for deployment)
      |
      +--------------> Streaming path (FraudScorer, windowed rules)
      |                     | fraud_alerts
      |                     v
      |               Live alerts + metrics (JSONL)
      v
 Medallion warehouse (DuckDB)
      Bronze (raw, append) --> PII classifier + manifest --> Silver (dedup,
      typed, PII-hashed) --> Gold (customer_360, order_facts, fraud_summary)
      |
      v
 Governance: erasure service + audit log + quality gate + Parquet lake`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section">
      <h2>Run it in sixty seconds</h2>
      <pre><code class="language-bash">{`git clone https://github.com/swadhin/eurostream && cd eurostream
uv sync
uv run eurostream demo`}</code></pre>
      <p>
        The demo is deterministic — it resets its data directory first — so you
        can run it repeatedly and diff the results. Stage 5 of the output is
        the point:
      </p>
      <pre><code>{`5/6 verifying cascade...
  bronze PII anonymized rows: 60 (before: 60 clear-text)
  gold customer_360 rows remaining: 0 (expect 0)
  audit log entries: 1 (expect 1)
  verification: PASSED`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section">
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Data / platform engineers</strong> who need GDPR-era
          governance patterns beyond "we have a retention policy".
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Backend engineers</strong> building event-driven systems who
          want the bus, contracts and quality-gate mechanics without a Kafka
          cluster.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Candidates preparing for interviews</strong> — every design
          decision here is a story: constraint → options → decision →
          consequence.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
  .landing {
    max-width: 60rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .landing-intro {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
    padding-inline-start: 1rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
  }
  .landing-section {
    margin-block-end: 2.5rem;
  }
  .landing-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-block-end: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
